.TH UNITOTEM-MANAGER 8 "October 2026" "unitotem-manager" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
unitotem-manager \- UniTotem kiosk scheduler and web management interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B unitotem-manager
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Starts the scheduler, the HTTPS API with the web interface (ports 443, and 80 redirecting to it) and, when
unitotem-viewer is installed and a display is available, one viewer window per screen. It is normally started
by the unitotem-manager.service unit.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-create\-admin " NAME"
Create the administrator
.I NAME
(or give an existing user a new password and the administrator capability), then exit. Must be run as root, with the
service stopped. The password is asked on the terminal, or read from the standard input when it is not a terminal
(\fBecho "$PASSWORD" | unitotem-manager --create-admin NAME\fR); it is never taken from the command line. The usual
password rules apply. It is also the way back in when nobody can log in.
.TP
.B \-\-no_gui true
Headless: run only the backend, without the local windows.
.SH FIRST ACCESS
A node carries no default account or password. Until an administrator exists the node is
.IR unclaimed :
its web interface only offers the setup page, where the person at the device enters a claim code and chooses the
administrator's username and password (and, optionally, the password of the operating-system account used by the
web terminal). The claim code is shown on the screen of the device, and for a device without a screen it is logged at
WARNING level and written to
.I /var/lib/unitotem/claim-code
(readable by root only, removed once the node is claimed). Resetting the users from the backup page returns the node to
this state, with a new code.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/unitotem/claim-code
The claim code of an unclaimed node.
.TP
.I /etc/unitotem
Configuration, playlists, users and pairing data.
.TP
.I /var/lib/unitotem/uploaded
Uploaded files.
.TP
.I /etc/ssl/unitotem.pem
Certificate and key of the web interface, created at installation.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/a13ssandr0/unitotem-manager
